  "title": "Contract and agency issue spotting",
  "html": "<div class=\"course-intro-card\"><h2>Contract and agency issue spotting</h2><p>Classify four independent business-law scenarios under the supplied ordinary legal principles.</p></div><section class=\"quiz-card\"><h3>Required responses</h3><div class=\"tbs-question\"><label for=\"reg-m2-tbs1-f1\">Authority in A</label><select id=\"reg-m2-tbs1-f1\"><option value=\"Actual authority\">Actual authority</option><option value=\"Only apparent authority from the agent\">Only apparent authority from the agent</option><option value=\"No authority\">No authority</option><option value=\"Ratification only\">Ratification only</option></select></div><div class=\"tbs-question\"><label for=\"reg-m2-tbs1-f2\">Authority in B</label><select id=\"reg-m2-tbs1-f2\"><option value=\"Apparent authority\">Apparent authority</option><option value=\"An agent’s unilateral invention of authority\">An agent’s unilateral invention of authority</option><option value=\"No possible authority\">No possible authority</option><option value=\"Only a tax agency\">Only a tax agency</option></select></div><div class=\"tbs-question\"><label for=\"reg-m2-tbs1-f3\">Doctrine in C</label><select id=\"reg-m2-tbs1-f3\"><option value=\"Ratification\">Ratification</option><option value=\"Automatic discharge in bankruptcy\">Automatic discharge in bankruptcy</option><option value=\"Novation in every case\">Novation in every case</option><option value=\"No possible adoption\">No possible adoption</option></select></div><div class=\"tbs-question\"><label for=\"reg-m2-tbs1-f4\">Recoverable loss after the stated mitigation adjustment</label><input id=\"reg-m2-tbs1-f4\" type=\"text\"></div></section>",
